                    <msContents>
                        <!-- describe the intellectual content of an inscription -->
                        <summary>From ARE 1927, 60: Records an agreement between Iḷaiya-perumāḷ-piḷḷai, Sundarattōḷ-piḷḷai and the tānattār of Tiruchchendūr for the merit of the former as kōvilkaṭṭaḷai. The gifted land is said to have been purchased and given to the tāṉattār of the temple. Kaḷappirāṉ the nephew of Raṅganātha-piḷḷai, the nāṭṭūkkaṇakku, seems to have drafted the document.</summary>
                        <!-- offers the possibility to give a summary of the inscription's content -->
                    </msContents>
                    <physDesc>
                        <handDesc>
                            <p>The inscription is filled with symbols and abbreviations. The same abbreviation seems to be used for <foreign>ṟ=ṟa</foreign> and <foreign>t=ta</foreign>. The abbreviations for <foreign>yu=M</foreign> seems to be used for <foreign>ya=M</foreign> as well. </p>
                            
                        </handDesc>
                    </physDesc>
                </msDesc>
